#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179559 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd087cbc-c76f-5900-a1ef-183c383e34ed" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Unlike Denominators"}] :question/id #uuid "bcf37a88-0ac3-59ca-8d23-8075f3eab872" :question/math-academy-id "e-9399" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $\\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{5}{6}$." :question/worked-solution "We write\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nas\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{6}\n$$\n\nand then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{6} - \\dfrac{5}{6} = \\dfrac{2 - 5}{6}\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2 - 5$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/c6/c63a3db44b79e751c7cf1a49dcebcbb1d00cea0427da4ef271d07646e4be2748.png)\n\nSo we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2 - 5}{6} = \\dfrac{-3}{6} = -\\dfrac{3}{6}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{3}{6} = -\\dfrac{3 \\div 3}{6 \\div 3} =-\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{5}{6} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179560 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179698 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ce776ed-33ba-522b-9241-68458339ddc6" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Unlike Denominators That Are Not Multiples"}] :question/id #uuid "5b669372-7867-597f-a28f-806aa47fbb2b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9400" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $\\dfrac{1}{4} - \\dfrac{5}{6}$." :question/worked-solution "We write\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nas\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{12}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{6}\n$$\n\nas\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{10}{12}\n$$\n\nand then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{12} - \\dfrac{10}{12} = \\dfrac{3 - 10}{12}\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $3 - 10$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/f4/f4dc7569aa731c13cf150d867479704cc46cbf7d6502cda4100538b4b2a7e9dc.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3 - 10}{12} = \\dfrac{-7}{12} = -\\dfrac{7}{12}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179561 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4a7fa46-e97d-5844-9d3d-8ba67d97cba2" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Mixed Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "d8350368-1542-53bc-9275-a1e1ff0a30d6" :question/math-academy-id "e-9401" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\dfrac{1}{3} - 2\\,\\dfrac{2}{3}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we write\n\n$$\n2 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nas an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2 \\,\\dfrac{2}{3} = \\dfrac{(2 \\times 3) + 2}{3} = \\dfrac{8}{3}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} - \\dfrac{8}{3} = \\dfrac{1 - 8}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $1 - 8$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/74/74047d21ae2b703b9962b9655eacbe2eee1a8d94fa4fd36a2924a6b02601d4fa.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1 - 8}{3} = \\dfrac{-7}{3} = -\\dfrac{7}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{7}{3} = -2 \\, \\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179562 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff50fccc-b442-5847-8029-2ca3be89c018" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "2472cc95-46be-56ac-811c-dd4982bc396f" :question/math-academy-id "e-9403" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\dfrac{5}{12} - \\dfrac{11}{12}$." :question/worked-solution "Since both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{12} - \\dfrac{11}{12} = \\dfrac{5 - 11}{12}\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $5 - 11$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/d9/d9367da101187cf8861458e58f16ea179cff66477d1b9060d3ae199ff8bb3843.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5 - 11}{12} = \\dfrac{-6}{12} = -\\dfrac{6}{12}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{6}{12} = -\\dfrac{6 \\div 6}{12 \\div 6} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{12} - \\dfrac{11}{12} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4a7fa46-e97d-5844-9d3d-8ba67d97cba2" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fraction: Mixed Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a275a266-d5d3-5599-9707-0f3c48df54fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177250} {:answer/id #uuid "f8231514-b107-5c9d-bb96-1b41c38a96f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177251} {:answer/id #uuid "20c944af-d01f-54b0-bedd-0f27397bd84a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177252} {:answer/id #uuid "254accaa-ba4e-57d5-8013-952e6e54ed0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177253} {:answer/id #uuid "67f35c3a-348d-5732-a6d4-914642be34c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177254}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f5c03ac6-fe73-511b-adc0-dfa8540d7eb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177249}] :question/id #uuid "affb9763-c3eb-526b-a6b6-46ddc9c223a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-119393" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\frac{2}{5} - 1\\frac{1}{5}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4a7fa46-e97d-5844-9d3d-8ba67d97cba2" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Positive Fraction From a Fra